From: UCU map kit <ucu-map-kit@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:11:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(export): default ShaderExportMode to Yaml

Shaders export as Unity YAML ShaderAssets (ShaderLab source plus the compiled programs) instead of the Dummy stand-in,
which the Unity 6 Editor can recompile.
---
 Source/AssetRipper.Export/Configuration/ExportSettings.cs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/AssetRipper.Export/Configuration/ExportSettings.cs b/Source/AssetRipper.Export/Configuration/ExportSettings.cs
index 18bc656c1..3942a2264 100644
--- a/Source/AssetRipper.Export/Configuration/ExportSettings.cs
+++ b/Source/AssetRipper.Export/Configuration/ExportSettings.cs
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ public sealed record class ExportSettings
 	/// <summary>
 	/// How to export shaders?
 	/// </summary>
-	public ShaderExportMode ShaderExportMode { get; set; } = ShaderExportMode.Dummy;
+	public ShaderExportMode ShaderExportMode { get; set; } = ShaderExportMode.Yaml;
 
 	/// <summary>
 	/// Should sprites be exported as a texture? Recommended: Native
